  "result": "I've looked through the site. It builds the timetable page from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and the site has no warnings yet. The file also only updates overnight, so a cancellation made during the day wouldn't reach the site until the next export.\n\nSo the main open question is where the cancellation news would come from. That decides whether this is a small change to how the site reads the file or a new way for someone to post updates during the day.\n\nWhen a sailing gets cancelled today, how does that news travel, and who knows first?\n\nOr if you'd rather I just dive in, say so.",
